# 17. Practical Implementation — Text Classification 📧

This is one of the most important Naive Bayes use cases.

## Step 1: Convert Text into Numbers

Machine Learning models cannot directly understand raw text.

We can use:

> **CountVectorizer**

```python
from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer
```

Example:

```text
Email Text
     ↓
CountVectorizer
     ↓
Word Frequency Matrix
     ↓
Multinomial Naive Bayes
```

---

## Complete Example

```python
from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer
from sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB

emails = [
    "Win free money now",
    "Meeting at 10 tomorrow",
    "Claim your free prize",
    "Project discussion tomorrow",
    "Win money quickly"
]

labels = [
    "spam",
    "ham",
    "spam",
    "ham",
    "spam"
]

# Convert text to numerical features
vectorizer = CountVectorizer()

X = vectorizer.fit_transform(emails)

# Train model
model = MultinomialNB()

model.fit(X, labels)

# Predict new email
new_email = [
    "Win free money"
]

new_X = vectorizer.transform(new_email)

prediction = model.predict(new_X)

print(prediction)
```

Expected concept:

```text
spam
```

